    "authors": [
      {
        "affiliation": "Sony Broadcast Limited Basingstoke, Hants, UK",
        "bio": "Jim Wilkinson completed his education at Sheffield Polytechnic in 1972. From then until 1974 he worked for Marconi Elliott Avionics on aircraft display systems. In 1974 he joined the Independent Broadcasting Authority and worked initially on the DICE digital standards converter. Subsequent projects were mainly concerned with digital video transmission and recording. In 1978 he joined Sony Broadcast to work in the newly created R&D team. Since then he has worked on a number of digital video recorder projects as well as various analogue and digital aspects of video processing. He is a member of the SMPTE, IEE, AES, and RTS.",
        "name": "James H. Wilkinson"
      }
